  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Huntington Ingalls obligated $2.8B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date, across 59 awards with an average award size of $47.1M. Obligations are down 33.7% year over year. Ship Building and Repairing is by far the largest market, accounting for $2.7B of obligations in the current fiscal year to date. Engineering Services accounted for $58.4M, Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance accounted for $39.1M, and Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing accounted for $7.5M in FY2026 to date. Looking at the recent fiscal history, obligations were $3.6B in FY21, $3B in FY22, $3.2B in FY23, $3.6B in FY24, and $4.2B in FY25. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations, while award-value figures in specific tables are total contract values. This snapshot shows where federal spending for Huntington Ingalls is concentrated and how the company’s FY2026 to date obligations compare with several prior fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Huntington Ingalls' federal revenue changed year over year?",
        "body": "Huntington Ingalls' obligations fell 33.7% year over year in FY2026 to date. Fiscal obligations rose from $3.6B in FY21 to $4.2B in FY25, then moved to $2.8B in FY26 to date. The FY2026 to date total is partial and covers the current fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do Huntington Ingalls' federal obligations concentrate?",
        "body": "Ship Building and Repairing is the largest market for Huntington Ingalls with $2.7B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services is the next market with $58.4M, followed by Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance with $39.1M and Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing with $7.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Huntington Ingalls make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Huntington Ingalls received $2.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company won 59 awards in the same period with an average award size of $47.1M. Fiscal obligations were $3.6B in FY21, $3B in FY22, $3.2B in FY23, $3.6B in FY24, and $4.2B in FY25 for context."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Huntington Ingalls?",
      "a": "The Department-level buyers are not listed on this page. The page shows market-level detail with Ship Building and Repairing receiving $2.7B, Engineering Services receiving $58.4M, Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance receiving $39.1M, and Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing receiving $7.5M in FY2026 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Huntington Ingalls sell to the government?",
      "a": "Huntington Ingalls sells ship building and repair services to the government, as shown by $2.7B in obligations for Ship Building and Repairing in FY2026 to date. The company also provides Engineering Services ($58.4M), Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance ($39.1M), and Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing ($7.5M) in the current fiscal year to date."
    },
